# ID: DET-09b
# Name: PowerShell with an encoded command (tuned)
# Purpose: Same as DET-09a with the known-good inventory agent excluded.
# Data: index=soc_lab sourcetype=sysmon:json EventCode=1
# MITRE ATT&CK: T1059.001 PowerShell; T1027 Obfuscated Files or Information
# Reference implementation: detections/reference_detections.py::encoded_powershell (with exclude_parent_images)
# Expected on the synthetic datasets: One event at 11:30:14 (the agent at 09:00:30 is excluded).
# False positives: An attacker could run PowerShell from the excluded parent path; exclude on the full path and hash, not only the file name.
# Tuning: Review the exclusion list regularly.
# Status: NOT TESTED in Splunk. The detection logic is tested in Python; the SPL syntax and field extractions need validation in a real Splunk.
# Lines that start with "#" are documentation. Paste only the lines below the blank line into the Splunk search bar.

index=soc_lab sourcetype=sysmon:json EventCode=1 Image="*\\powershell.exe"
| regex CommandLine="(?i)\s-(enc|encodedcommand|ec)\s"
| search NOT ParentImage="*\\HarborInventory\\agent.exe"
| table _time Computer User ParentImage CommandLine
| sort 0 _time
